.page sync 1 flush filesystem buffers

# SYNOPSIS
*sync*

# DESCRIPTION
`sync` asks the kernel to write pending changes to the storage devices.

If a disk refuses the writes (an I/O error), `sync` says so and exits with status 1; the changes stay in memory and the next `sync`, `umount` or the background writer tries again. `umount` refuses a volume that cannot be written back, and the kernel log (`dmesg`) names the disk and the failing sectors.

# EXIT STATUS
0 when everything was written, 1 when a write-back failed.

# SEE ALSO
dd(1), mount(8)
